      "content_index_zero_based": 11,
      "type": "text",
      "text_en": "Engaged stakeholders are a critical success factor to any significant change. And the earlier the engagement, the better the chances of success. This can be seen in most of the latest trends in development approaches such as Agile and DevOps. The Initial Verification phase takes the current premise, key questions, and targeted stakeholders and engages those stakeholders to validate and/or improve the understanding of the real problem and the real questions that need be addressed in order for a project to lead to a success.",
