    "type": "text",
    "text_en": "The preceding paragraphs highlight the conceptual scope of EA. This scope often leads to the assumption that EA is only used to answer the big questions. Nothing can be further from the truth. The same concepts, methods, techniques, and frameworks can readily be used to address the end state, preference trade-off, and value realization for big and little questions. The essential difference is not what you do; it is what the documented architecture looks like. The scope of the system varies; the detailed description of elements and properties vary. All of the concepts remain the same.",
    "source_block_ids": [
      "G186:p0026:b009",
      "G186:p0026:b010",
      "G186:p0026:b011",
      "G186:p0026:b012",
      "G186:p0026:b013",
      "G186:p0026:b014"
    ],
