      "description_zh": "第 3.2.1 节先写“Without performing repeated information gathering…cannot proceed”，随即强调既有决策与最少必要分析，容易误读为必须每次重复全部调查。译文保留原句；应用时结合其后限量原则，不静默改成 without repeating。",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source_unit_id": "G186:p0027:c003",
          "pdf_page": 27,
          "source_block_ids": [
            "G186:p0027:b014",
            "G186:p0027:b015",
            "G186:p0027:b016",
            "G186:p0027:b017",
            "G186:p0027:b018",
            "G186:p0027:b019",
            "G186:p0027:b020",
            "G186:p0027:b021"
          ],
          "quote_en": "When populated, the EA Landscape contains a description, constraints, or guidance that can be used. Without performing repeated information gathering, analysis, review, and approval, the Practitioner cannot proceed with confidence. Existing decisions, guidance, and constraints inform current architecture development. Best practice limits information gathering and analysis to the minimum necessary to address the question at hand. Effort spent on EA returns the highest value when the EA is used. The EA cannot be used until the architect is “done”. All architecture development must be assessed against Time-To-Market (TTM). Filling in only the required parts of the EA Landscape, and following the constraints and guidance already in place, speeds TTM.",
          "source_path": "togaf-standard-10th/G186e.pdf",
          "source_sha256": "ed1c26faba5023a8d1b32b0ec893d75a3bb1d7a6508e99fa56ded079585d922a"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
