          "G186:p0041:b018"
        ],
        "quote_en": "For most organizations, the budget cycle controls change in the organization. Pragmatically, the EA team will be aligned to the budget cycle. Figure 4-1 shows a timeline view, depicting an alignment of key decisions made during a business cycle and the purpose architectures. EA for Strategy, Portfolio, and Project need to be completed before key milestones for budget decisions are made. EA for Solution Delivery is a continuous operation around budget control. The key takeaway is architecture before the decision. If you are trapped trying to architect after the decision, see Section 11.2.1.",
        "source_path": "togaf-standard-10th/G186e.pdf",
        "source_sha256": "ed1c26faba5023a8d1b32b0ec893d75a3bb1d7a6508e99fa56ded079585d922a"
