          "quote_en": "The most common interpretations of trade-off are “a balance achieved between two desirable but incompatible features; a compromise” and “losing one quality, aspect, or amount of something in return for gaining another quality, aspect, or amount”. In developing an Enterprise Architecture, trade- offs are never about compromises where a middle ground is sought. Trade-off requires understanding the complete set of all stakeholder preferences and their interaction. Trade-off assesses a complex set of benefits and costs to find the optimal value point where all minimum benefits are included, and the highest total value is reached at an acceptable cost. Stakeholder concerns are critical in assessing",
          "source_path": "togaf-standard-10th/G186e.pdf",
          "source_sha256": "ed1c26faba5023a8d1b32b0ec893d75a3bb1d7a6508e99fa56ded079585d922a"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
