        "quote_en": "[1] Use of the term “desired” is intentional to communicate the fact that it is difficult for a human to foresee and consider change parameters in the future. Until a consensus is reached across key decision-makers, data gathered during assessment is an opinion or a wish. Once confirmed, it becomes a candidate target state. Once funded or signed off, it becomes the target state. [2] Superior architecture is an architecture that constrains, guides, and directs population of the EA Landscape within the scope of the Request for Architecture Work. Architecture to Support Strategy is the superior architecture for Architecture to Support Portfolio. Architecture to Support Portfolio is the superior architecture for the Architecture Project. The Architecture Project is the superior architecture for Architecture to Support Solution Delivery.",
