            "G21I:p0015:b035",
            "G21I:p0015:b036"
          ],
          "quote_en": "The concept of MSA is designed to simplify business operations and to promote the interoperability of the various parts of that business, in order to increase business agility. It is possible to easily define an organization’s functional capabilities by structuring capacity as meaningful, granular services as opposed to opaque, siloed business units, without duplicating similar capabilities across the organization. Precisely defined granularity, aligned with business domain and clearly defined interfaces, limits the impact of changes and allows understanding of mutual dependencies.",
          "source_path": "togaf-standard-10th/G21Ie.pdf",
          "source_sha256": "279f6c06124f49a147a168591965805115b2fc976eea2664e41e491ac5d163bf"
        }
      ]
    }
