        ],
        "quote_en": "Phase A is followed by the three TOGAF phases that produce detailed architecture descriptions for the Architecture Definition Document. In each of these phases, the architect:",
        "source_path": "togaf-standard-10th/G21Ie.pdf",
        "source_sha256": "279f6c06124f49a147a168591965805115b2fc976eea2664e41e491ac5d163bf"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "G21I:6.4:rule02",
    "kind": "source-semantic-rule",
    "statement_zh": "业务能力和功能须置于企业上下文，后续生命周期和治理聚焦特定功能变更。",
    "boundary_zh": "“变更程度应相当小”是来源预期，不是对变更规模的保证或拒绝重大变更的判据。",
    "evidence": [
      {
        "source_unit_id": "G21I:p0034:c014",
        "pdf_page": 34,
        "source_block_ids": [
          "G21I:p0034:b025",
          "G21I:p0034:b026",
          "G21I:p0034:b027",
          "G21I:p0034:b028"
        ],
        "quote_en": "For MSA, the individual business capability and functions that are being addressed should be defined in the context of the overall enterprise. This is particularly important when considerations of lifecycle and governance are addressed; these would only apply to changes to that particular business function. The degree of change should be fairly small after the initial Baseline Architecture has been created.",
        "source_path": "togaf-standard-10th/G21Ie.pdf",
        "source_sha256": "279f6c06124f49a147a168591965805115b2fc976eea2664e41e491ac5d163bf"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "G21I:6.4:rule03",
    "kind": "source-semantic-rule",
    "statement_zh": "每次架构工作在阶段 A 确认关键利益相关者、关注点、需求和应开发的视图与视角。",
    "boundary_zh": "不能为所有项目固定生成相同图集并声称已满足利益相关者需要。",
    "evidence": [
      {
        "source_unit_id": "G21I:p0034:c015",
        "pdf_page": 34,
        "source_block_ids": [
          "G21I:p0034:b029",
          "G21I:p0034:b030",
          "G21I:p0034:b031",
          "G21I:p0034:b032"
        ],
        "quote_en": "The requirements to address, the stakeholders to consult, and the models and views to develop vary from one architecture engagement to another. In Phase A of each engagement the architect identifies the key stakeholders and their concerns, states the key business requirements to be addressed, and considers which architecture views and viewpoints to develop.",
        "source_path": "togaf-standard-10th/G21Ie.pdf",
        "source_sha256": "279f6c06124f49a147a168591965805115b2fc976eea2664e41e491ac5d163bf"
      }
    ]
  }
