          "quote_en": "Phase C: Information Systems Architectures of the TOGAF ADM consists of two architecture domains for the project: the Data Architecture and the Application Architecture. In the context of an MSA, the applications generally consist of the services and operations exposed to service consumers and utilities used to maintain the services. Datadata is constrained to the data managed by the business function being served by the MSA and external data sources that may be used as an offline source or repository for such data.",
          "source_path": "togaf-standard-10th/G21Ie.pdf",
          "source_sha256": "279f6c06124f49a147a168591965805115b2fc976eea2664e41e491ac5d163bf"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
