          "quote_en": "Each microservice has a source unit. This source unit contains the code that implements the microservice’s ABF. It does not share code with other microservice source units, and cannot access their data. It may use libraries for functions that are not business-related. Each microservice also has a deployment unit that is built from its source unit and the libraries that the source unit uses. A deployment unit cannot include code for more than one microservice. Each microservice deployment unit is deployed as a single execution unit or, in a system at scale, multiple execution units running the same code.",
          "source_path": "togaf-standard-10th/G21Ie.pdf",
